                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">An early nineteenth-century script.</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red.</seg>
                        <desc>Rather mediocre but careful hand; squared characters. 
                           The ink on <locus target="#2 #3 #4r #6r #7 #8r #15v"/> has faded away. 
                           On some folia, the faded characters have been traced in blue and red ink for more legibility. 
                           The manuscript was copied by Gabra Ṣǝyon mentioned on <locus target="#2ra #20va #129r"/>), apparently the owner.</desc>
                      
                        <list type="abbreviations">
                           <item><abbr>ጊዮር፡</abbr> for <expan>ጊዮርጊስ፡</expan> (<locus target="#2ra"/>)</item>
                           <item>
                              <abbr>ዳለ፡</abbr> for <expan>እንዳለ፡</expan> (<locus target="#41vab #42ra #42vb #43vab #44rab #44vab #49rab #70rb #107ra"></locus>)
                           </item>
                        </list>
                      
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; beginning of sections and subsections;
                           names of the scribe and his (spiritual) ‘fathers’; corrections to the text, inserted
                           between the columns or interlineally (<locus target="#4v #42v #49r #52r #65r #69r"/>);
                           a few other words like <foreign xml:lang="gez">ʾOrit</foreign> (<locus target="#20r"/>), <foreign xml:lang="gez">ba-sǝmʿātǝm</foreign> (<locus target="#25v"/>), 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">nagar gǝn</foreign>(<locus target="#26r #30r"/>), <foreign xml:lang="gez">ʾahun</foreign> (<locus target="#2v"/>), 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">liqāwǝntǝmm</foreign> (<locus target="#26v"/>), <foreign xml:lang="gez">dagmom</foreign> (<locus target="#24v #25r #26v #28r #29v #30r"/>), 
                           and <foreign xml:lang="gez">yagǝd</foreign> (<locus target="#34r"/>); elements of  punctuation marks and sections dividers; elements of Ethiopic
                           numerals.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                     
                     <handNote xml:id="h2" script="Ethiopic">
                        <locus from="2r" to="71r">2r-71r</locus>: careful, though the hand is not
                        well-trained<!--The names of this hands need to be replaced by appropriate refs.--></handNote>
                     <handNote xml:id="h3" script="Ethiopic"> The quality of the handwriting
                        deteriorates on <locus from="71v" to="129r">71v-129r</locus>.<!--The names of this hands need to be replaced by appropriate refs.--></handNote>
                  </handDesc>
